interber - a web browser that looks like a tty
=============================================
The whole window is the page. One line at the bottom to type in, the
console's font and colours, and [ tabs ] on top when there's more than one:

	[ github ] [ youtube ]
	...the page...
	https://github.com/tortr-rs/chamesle                      42%

Type an address, or words to search. The home page is your bookmarks.

One C file on WebKitGTK, the same engine as surf and GNOME Web.

Install
-------
	make
	sudo make install

Settings
--------
~/.config/interber/config, made the first time interber starts. Plain words:

	home page = interber:home
	search = https://duckduckgo.com/?q=%s
	remember tabs = on
	javascript = on
	zoom = 100%
	downloads = ~/Downloads
	text colour = grey
	background colour = black

Change a line and save: it works from the next page you open.
Bookmarks are ~/.config/interber/bookmarks, one "address name" a line.

Keys
----
	Ctrl+l              type an address or a search
	Ctrl+t              new tab
	Ctrl+w              close tab
	Ctrl+Shift+t        bring the closed tab back
	Ctrl+Tab            next tab, Ctrl+1..9 a tab
	Alt+Left, Alt+Right back, forward
	Ctrl+r              reload
	Ctrl+f              find on the page, Enter for the next one
	Ctrl+d              bookmark the page
	Ctrl+plus, minus, 0 zoom
	F11                 full screen
	Ctrl+h              home
	Ctrl+q              quit

Middle click or Ctrl+click a link for a new tab, middle click a tab to close it.
Downloads go straight into ~/Downloads.
